          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dacfdb2ed3944a91b4f6aef60ae2ade433e3d1f245f3ffb8302f843b1ecca41e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_28d5156ae89c480ab5523ec9808de40e",
      "statement": "Turns (user messages) are durable before execution: turn runs store status, checkpoints, and lease metadata; runners mint leases with expiry time and heartbeats renew it; expired leases emit recovery events and converge to stable state (queued, cancelled, or failed).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/internal/reborn/contracts/turn-persistence.md#L26-L103",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:05e5a25bed59e9333e8598c5ab8a9c7ee764cadc8a17de044832e48b920f31c2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b5ba229056704fb8ae7ebd0fdcfa3e5f",
      "statement": "Turn admission reservations track capacity usage per tenant/actor/project/agent; all configured buckets are checked atomically with turn creation; reservations are released exactly once when run reaches terminal state; missing limits mean unlimited.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/internal/reborn/contracts/turn-persistence.md#L71-L83",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1a5932d646e1014241a35a0203e1d61c2e9a11259067bbc474eac902af095f0d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_002f5f258e494cffb08f11955cf7a827",
      "statement": "Released migrations are immutable; changes to production schema require new migrations (never edit released .sql files); all migrations must be idempotent and preserve multi-tenant isolation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/internal/reborn/contracts/migration-compatibility.md#L23-L32",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:16edd65af69f86aea930ffe2d5068cbfec67c0d288badd73a0ea98d74bafd970:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b369ce199f2f43439cd3bc5bd58b9f98",
      "statement": "Production migration policy: libSQL and PostgreSQL only; in-memory and JSONL rejected; remote PostgreSQL requires sslmode=require and explicit allow-remote-cleartext setting; TLS and durability validated before opening connections.",
